{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt","id":1236317,"title":"Crossover Issues/Doubt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-17T23:25:03-07:00","id":1236317,"title":"Crossover Issues/Doubt","content":"I plan to do a crossover-centric chronicle. But there are some problems. As I was reading the Core RuleBooks from each template, I was realizing that a Mage can get absurd results with only one success.<br /> <br /> So, I had some doubts: if any of the players eventually reached the Master level in at least one Arcanum (Life, for example), could he give One Hit Kill to a werewolf with only one success? If that is possible, I think this makes the crossover very unbalanced when compared to 1st Edition. Or am I missing something here? Is there any way to make things more balanced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7002-obrimosg-d","name":"ObrimosG'd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T23:58:49-07:00","id":1236323,"title":"","content":"No you are not missing anything. This was btw kind of the same for first edition. There was no problem using a Master level spell to instantly kill even a supernatural beeing in first edition. Non of the CoD implements are ment to be balanced with each other. If you want to run a crossover I would suggest to give the Mage characters less or some other splats more experience. I also would suggest not to let Mage PC get to Master level. They usually deal with problems, that are not very crossover friendly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T00:10:01-07:00","id":1236325,"title":"","content":"Salient question: Who are you crossing Mage over with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T01:39:46-07:00","id":1236335,"title":"","content":"Crossover is risky business.<br /> <br /> The splats were designed with internal balance in mind, and in a compatible way so that they could be used as NPCs in each other's Chronicles.<br /> e.g. The Mage busybody that just won't leave the Demon alone, the arrogant Vampire who bites off more than he can chew with a pack of Uratha<br /> <br /> But external balance? No way, man.<br /> Mages take for granted powers that other splats would kill for, and routinely solve problems they'd struggle with, even before the fourth dot in an Arcanum.<br /> It's important to be aware of that when running crossover. Where each dot grants other splats a power or two, for Mages it gives a loosely defined swathe.<br /> <br /> *edit*<br /> I have no suggestions for making it more balanced, many of a Mage's strengths go right to the core of the splat, and removing/altering them is like knocking down the foundations of a building, it screws with the other assumptions built on them.<br /> I'd suggest a gentleman's agreement instead. A little mutual respect can solve a lot of problems, including PC power disparity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T02:07:28-07:00","id":1236339,"title":"","content":"Or... the problem is solved fairly easily. Let the werewolf make a pact with some gulmoth - or even as its totem, although that might be a dark chronicle - and the gulmoth can influence magic/paradox with its influence/numina. More horror, more in theme, and gulmoths allow you to suture the two games together. Or get the gulmoth sit in a fetish to give protection against one-hit kills. And remember, the mage's true bane is ambush.<br /> <br /> The imbalance is always overblown on paper, where the deck can be indefinitely stacked. In gameplay, I have not found it to be a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T02:52:54-07:00","id":1236342,"title":"","content":"I recall an anecdote by a poster here (Acrozatarim, IIRC) where they had two or three fish-monster things with Forces 5 as enemies to fight against a pack of Uratha. He said Forces 5 only barely kept them toe-to-toe with the pack. Now, I probably am misremembering a few details... but the point is that mages might not be that hard to fight against. <br /> <br /> There\u2019s also the Counterspell (Countermagic?) Numen from Dark Eras. Have a bunch of ephemerals/Horrors spam them. <br /> <br /> Or we can crank up the crossover-ness and involve the Guardians and the Seers. They tend to get involved when mages go around throwing spells willy-nilly. And often, siccing a mage is the best solution against a wayward mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T03:16:35-07:00","id":1236348,"title":"","content":"Yes - counterspell as a numen may help.<br /> <br /> Also - thinking of why the two games combine is useful. If there is indeed a rise in spirits/gulmoth with countermagic abilities, werewolves might be the most valuable asset of the awakened in the region: giving the splats a reason to combo.<br /> <br /> One other thing though; mage combat in our group has always been rocket tag; one or two hits and you are out, with little comeback, even with magic. To avoid annhiliation, Beaten Down tilt has been narratively useful. However, werewolf is more capable of drawn out brawls - where their staying power is great. So - rather than see this as a dissonance in the combat styles of the two games, it can be a chance for both to shine. If the problem can be resolved in a blast or two, great. If it lasts longer, it will be good to have the werewolf in grappling it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T03:26:49-07:00","id":1236349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt?p=1236342#post1236342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall an anecdote by a poster here (Acrozatarim, IIRC) where they had two or three fish-monster things with Forces 5 as enemies to fight against a pack of Uratha. He said Forces 5 only barely kept them toe-to-toe with the pack. Now, I probably am misremembering a few details... but the point is that mages might not be that hard to fight against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under most circumstance, if the mage (or other user with a 5 dot in Arcana) is able to use a single spell, a point of willpower and without problem about 20 people are unmade without any clash of wills or anything like it. But yes, in a 'real' scenario mages are far from the OP-ness they are generally described as. But, as with most dangerous foes, if you outnumber them, you'll probably win. The question is, how much is it going to cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There\u2019s also the Counterspell (Countermagic?) Numen from Dark Eras. Have a bunch of ephemerals/Horrors spam them. </div> </div> </div>To be fairly honest about the Countermagic numen, it doesn't seem to be all to common either, and the rules a tid bit broken.<br /> <br /> But back to OP, well mages are usually more powerful then most splats and more versatile, but they get another powerspike at Arcana 4 and one yet again at 5. More then a few in the mage community seem to be under the impression that normal play is pretty much impossible when you reach that level on arcane knowledge because most things cease to be a problem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:39:01-07:00","id":1236424,"title":"","content":"The problem most STs have with Mage is that they try to run it like other games. They try to make problems that are fairly straight-forward with obvious objectives because in most other games the characters lack the power to simply will the solution into existence.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of of ways to slow Mages down. Do not give them a lot of time. Give them problems that are made up of multiple parts split across time, space and invisible worlds. Give them problems with more than one active piece in play at a time. Give them more than one problem at a time. Let them lead themselves into thinking they're dealing with one kind of problem that is actually a different kind of problem. Create problems with multiple solutions, each with different payoffs and sacrifices. Make use of their various antagonists and social pressures. <br /> <br /> None of this makes a Mage less powerful, but it does make it possible run a game with Mages in it. If you're using a Mage as an antagonist, then the players should be made aware that they need to attack the Mage as on as many fronts in as varied a way as possible if they want an easier time of it. Although, if the Mage is working alone then just having the numbers advantage may be enough. If the Mage is one player character in a group of player characters then eventually as the Mage grows you are probably going to need Mage level problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:53:03-07:00","id":1236432,"title":"","content":"The splats are made to be internally consistent, balancing them against each other would take a lot of homebrewing, experimenting, frustration and even then it might make certain players feel the powers they imagined fall short. A game like D&amp;D is designed from the ground up to not only be there to tell stories, but also to be a war game, running the numbers, optimizing and seeing the ensuing absurdity is part of what builds the experience. CofD is designed to be more focused on telling great stories. So I propose a paradigm shift: seek perfect imbalance. Here are some thoughts about how to do it:<br /> <br /> 1- Have each player fill a niche. A werewolf Ithaeur and a Thrysus can both fill the spirit shaman role, yet the Thrysus will have a harder time because, even with an honorary spirit rank, because he is an outsider, so he needs to play a dangerous game of bribes, coercion and intimidation that the werewolf are much more equipped to deal with, but as he reaches Mastery this could invert. That would make it so one of them will always feel like a dead weight at some point. But if they each have a different focus, that changes entirely. The Eleventh Question can be the detective, the Daeva can be the face of the party, the Rahu can be the combat specialist, and so on, there are many ways to go about it, the splats are flexible enough to accommodate all types of builds. Now when their powers peak, each player will feel satisfied and you will have a balanced party, ready too tackle any complex problems you send their way.<br /> <br /> 2- One of the coolest things about the Chronicles of Darkness is that there is always a bigger fish. If the players go too overt with the power displays, then they have to deal with the consequences. Maybe you called the attention of an Stryx, or disturbed a Seer operation, or that artifact you stole belonged to a mummy's cult, maybe that street gang's operation was unknowing infrastructure to the God Machine or maybe an archmage saw some interesting new pawns. Let them be free to make their choices, but be bound by the consequences.<br /> <br /> 3- Remember that each splat comes with drawbacks. Mages are crazy flexible, but they are also very squishy if caught off guard. A werewolf can heal quickly or become a death machine, a vampire has a tough undead body, a Geist just comes back from death and a Promethean is a juggernaut that can heal with electricity. Sure you can kill werewolves at high Arcanum, but do you have the mana to keep doing it if things escalate ? What happens if the attacker is a vampire who sent armed Sleeper thugs or an Obrimos who also warded them with Prime ? Are you sure you should be Reaching that much ? The Paradox just keeps building. By the same token, the method a werewolf used to keep Harmony in balance might go against the Oath of The Moon, or it might be fine with it but be a horrendous act by human standards, certainly illegal. Having to deal with those helps flesh out a character.<br /> <br /> 4- What is good enough for the players is good enough for the antagonists. So they braved the Shadow version of the villain's hideout to get the McGuffin ? Hopefully they covered their tracks. Otherwise ghosts will slowly scout the city for it, and when they find it, the Geist behind it will slowly have them posses the neighboring people and, when the time is right, spring an attack on the player's base. While they are dealing with it, they sneak by Twilight and take the items back. Hold on, where is the Beast ? Your player's phone rings, its from their house, its going to be one of those night.<br /> <br /> \u200bHope that is helps. What splats are you utilizing ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-18-2018, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:45:40-07:00","id":1236473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObrimosG'd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt#post1236317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I plan to do a crossover-centric chronicle. But there are some problems. As I was reading the Core RuleBooks from each template, I was realizing that a Mage can get absurd results with only one success.<br /> <br /> So, I had some doubts: if any of the players eventually reached the Master level in at least one Arcanum (Life, for example), could he give One Hit Kill to a werewolf with only one success? If that is possible, I think this makes the crossover very unbalanced when compared to 1st Edition. Or am I missing something here? Is there any way to make things more balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage can one shot with Mastery. Aka: Gnosi 5 AND Arcana a 5. A pc with power stat at 5 and a Power at 5 is a powerfull character in every line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:52:57-07:00","id":1236477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt?p=1236424#post1236424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem most STs have with Mage is that they try to run it like other games. They try to make problems that are fairly straight-forward with obvious objectives because in most other games the characters lack the power to simply will the solution into existence.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of of ways to slow Mages down. Do not give them a lot of time. Give them problems that are made up of multiple parts split across time, space and invisible worlds. Give them problems with more than one active piece in play at a time. Give them more than one problem at a time. Let them lead themselves into thinking they're dealing with one kind of problem that is actually a different kind of problem. Create problems with multiple solutions, each with different payoffs and sacrifices. Make use of their various antagonists and social pressures. <br /> <br /> None of this makes a Mage less powerful, but it does make it possible run a game with Mages in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sooo... basically bless them with the luck of Harry Blackstone Copperfield Dresden? =p<br /> <br /> <br /> Need to second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> here: Tips will be much more helpful if we know the splats involved. Most here assume it is werewolf, due to your example.<br /> The general idea stays the same, of course: give each splat Chances to play towards their strengths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T11:00:06-07:00","id":1236481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt?p=1236477#post1236477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo... basically bless them with the luck of Harry Blackstone Copperfield Dresden? =p<br /> <br /> Need to second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> here: Tips will be much more helpful if we know the splats involved. Most here assume it is werewolf, due to your example.<br /> The general idea stays the same, of course: give each splat Chances to play towards their strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or worse if you can manage it.<br /> <br /> I don't know that there really needs to be information about the other splats. The &quot;problem&quot; is with Mage. Once you clear up how to run Mage incorporating other splats is fairly easy I think since they basically fall into Mage's vast spectrum of cryptids. Which is not saying that Mage is superior, simply that other splats tend to be more straightforward and obvious about how they go about solving problems and the kinds of problems they focus on due to their limitations or powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:28:45-07:00","id":1236511,"title":"","content":"My advise about crossovers involving mage is don't do it.<br /> <br /> Ok more seriously, aside from what has been mentioned by others before, crossovers with a mage pc only work if the player of the mage ooc handles his power responsibly. Meaning building his char in a way that he has weakspots other members of the party can support, thus keeping them &quot;relevant&quot;. Alternativly it can be a game where the mage is overpowering all other chars, such as a mage and his/her cultists.... but that aswell requires much maturity from all players. If you have a mage and say a vampire in a party then the mage is going to be more powerful if they have any imagination, this is a fact that all players need to know and accept before play starts. If that leads to unease... best not have a mage in your party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:42:45-07:00","id":1236516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObrimosG'd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt#post1236317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that is possible, I think this makes the crossover very unbalanced when compared to 1st Edition. Or am I missing something here? Is there any way to make things more balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't different in first edition, the games were not made to be played together like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:53:06-07:00","id":1236520,"title":"","content":"Either homebrew some stuff to dial Mage back (unmaking spells work differently in my games, though that's not exactly 100% of the problem you're facing), or more strictly limit the player's Gnosis/Arcana. I'm a big fan of Mage, but it's got some crossover issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:20:34-07:00","id":1236534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt?p=1236342#post1236342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall an anecdote by a poster here (Acrozatarim, IIRC) where they had two or three fish-monster things with Forces 5 as enemies to fight against a pack of Uratha. He said Forces 5 only barely kept them toe-to-toe with the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Must've been pulling punches, then, or there's more context we're missing. Eradicate Energy with Advanced Scale = no more Pack. Each of them is going to Withstand with Stamina (which is boosted via Shapeshifting), but even before adding spell factors the thing would be at 5 Potency, and each subject Withstands <i>separately</i>.<br /> <br /> @OP Crossover balance has never been a priority, and the talk about Mages reaching 5 dots to be able to 1-shot isn't even setting the proper expectations: It's pretty easy to kill someone with a couple dots in a few different Arcana, and while Uratha are going to be more resistant to some of those methods than others, they aren't resistant to all of them; eg. Psychic Domination.<br /> <br /> If you're concerned about balance, Mage probably isn't the best game to include in your crossover. That said, I've had plenty of crossover games with them where everything worked out fine, but balance has never been a large concern for my group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T14:29:10-07:00","id":1236560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt?p=1236534#post1236534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must've been pulling punches, then, or there's more context we're missing. Eradicate Energy with Advanced Scale = no more Pack. Each of them is going to Withstand with Stamina (which is boosted via Shapeshifting), but even before adding spell factors the thing would be at 5 Potency, and each subject Withstands <i>separately</i>.<br /> <br /> @OP Crossover balance has never been a priority, and the talk about Mages reaching 5 dots to be able to 1-shot isn't even setting the proper expectations: It's pretty easy to kill someone with a couple dots in a few different Arcana, and while Uratha are going to be more resistant to some of those methods than others, they aren't resistant to all of them; eg. Psychic Domination.<br /> <br /> If you're concerned about balance, Mage probably isn't the best game to include in your crossover. That said, I've had plenty of crossover games with them where everything worked out fine, but balance has never been a large concern for my group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops, turns out I completely misremembered that anecdote, everyone. I searched it, and it\u2019s about how one of The Deeps isn\u2019t a match for an Uratha pack despite its stats on paper, and that Acrozatarim had to deploy two of those things and a Forces Master to match the \u201cencounter level\u201d as I describe it. <br /> <br /> So yeah, Masters are terrifying. Still no mentions of a one-hit-kill, so there\u2019s probably more context missing. <br /> <br /> I suppose another way of integrating this power level discrepancy is... acknowledging it in-universe. I mean, don\u2019t the games do anyways? The Stereotypes sections mention how the other supernaturals are wary of mages. And people prepare for danger, yes? Seems like supernaturals would have figured out counter-mage tactics by now, like burning anything that can serve as a sympathetic link, sniping from afar, purposedly going into frenzy/Kuruth in a fight, meeting them where there are lots of normal people, not meeting them in person in the first place, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T12:32:06-07:00","id":1237228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObrimosG'd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt#post1236317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I plan to do a crossover-centric chronicle. But there are some problems. As I was reading the Core RuleBooks from each template, I was realizing that a Mage can get absurd results with only one success.<br /> <br /> So, I had some doubts: if any of the players eventually reached the Master level in at least one Arcanum (Life, for example), could he give One Hit Kill to a werewolf with only one success? If that is possible, I think this makes the crossover very unbalanced when compared to 1st Edition. Or am I missing something here? Is there any way to make things more balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div> To be fair, so can changelings, who if they drop the mask get an exceptional success as long as they succeed on contract rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:03:10-07:00","id":1237254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt?p=1237228#post1237228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, so can changelings, who if they drop the mask get an exceptional success as long as they succeed on contract rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget, is that still in 2E?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:14:49-07:00","id":1237262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt?p=1237254#post1237254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget, is that still in 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. Embracing the Wyrd is the thing that's gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T20:05:16-07:00","id":1237383,"title":"","content":"But many contracts don't have a roll at all anymore, making that power more limited in application than it was in earlier drafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T20:38:35-07:00","id":1237389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt?p=1237383#post1237383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But many contracts don't have a roll at all anymore, making that power more limited in application than it was in earlier drafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also now explicitly offers a benefit to those Contracts in this circumstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T21:11:25-07:00","id":1237398,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7002-obrimosg-d\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7002\" data-vbnamecard=\"7002\">ObrimosG'd</a>, if you want more balanced <b>CoD</b> game as crossover friendly in setting as <b>Mage</b> - I propose <b>Beast: The Priordrial</b>. It's <i>highly</i> based on Astral Space ( like parts of <b>Mage</b> ), encourage cooperation with other monsters ( even mechanical ) - and is much more manageable, power-wise, on general. <b>Beast </b>also share with <b>Mage</b> a lot of themes - like Mystery seeking ( for getting new Lairs Chambers or finding Dark Mother ). Also, using one or two Awakened PCs in <b>Beast</b> game is totally fine - and with only 1 or 2 mage characters, you can more easily uncover their drawbacks in stories.<br /> <br /> Yes, <b>Beast</b> was secret crossover game I thought <b>Mage</b> was for whole 12+ years - that I always IMAGINED <b>Mage</b> could be, but internal <b>Mage</b> mechanics made them unplayable in long term. Go figure that... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-21-2018, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T01:57:56-07:00","id":1237439,"title":"","content":"While Beast is mechanically designed to promote crossover games, its tone is either less than universally applicable for its partner splats, or so bland that it can only find identity by leeching onto the other game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T11:20:01-07:00","id":1237545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1236317-crossover-issues-doubt?p=1237439#post1237439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Beast is mechanically designed to promote crossover games, its tone is either less than universally applicable for its partner splats, or so bland that it can only find identity by leeching onto the other game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>You clearly did not read <b>Beast Players Guide</b> - this books changes EVERYTHING in reception of this gameline. I was<i> literally</i> thrown away by <b>Beast</b> corebook - but reading <b>BPG</b> gives you soooo muuuch inter-<b>Beast</b> setting and ideas - I plan to run <b>Beast </b>in Edinburgh ( with big dash of <b>Geist</b> ) as my next big chronicle, after <b>Werewolf </b>now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> in <b>BPG</b> you got things like:<ul><li><b>New Families and Hungers </b>- yay, for Inguma, doppelgangers and infiltrators blending with humanity and still creeping it. ( Like aliens invading you suburbs or Fear of Other in general. ) Or Hungers for Secrets and Transgresions ( called Tempeters, like demons ).</li> <li><b>Horrorspawns</b> - Mini-Beasts from your Horrors that can work for you. Also, you can 'mentally reproduction' with other Beasts to have more powerful Spawns! ( Very <i>Neon Genesis Evangelion</i>-like! )</li> <li><b>Astral Space rules and setting from POV of Beasts</b>. And it's VERY different than mages perspective.</li> <li><b>Mysteries and clues of workings of Dark Mother</b> - and ritualistic magic of Beasts, based on Her blessings.</li> <li>Clearly description how Beast should work as gameline.</li> <li>New powers, Merits, and a like.</li> </ul>Really, <b>BPG</b> should be called <b>Beast Corebook, Part 2</b>, in my POV! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-21-2018, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}